 really really really really really works  and again you have to be willing to give  up the small wings to go for the big  wins number six is value your time I  don't think people value their time  enough  I don't think entrepreneurs value their  time enough if I audited your date and  look at what you were actually doing  during the day there'd be a lot of waste  of time all the time you spend on  Facebook or clicking refresh on your  statistics to see how many people watch  your YouTube videos in the past hour and  going back and check in again or check  in your sales numbers over and over and  over and over again yes you could work  harder yes you can add more hours to  your day because you need to get more  work done but I would say that a huge  chunk of your current day even if you  work 0 extra hours could be way more  productive because you're just not  focused and that's a harsh truth that's  something that's hard to say and hard to  realize but if you look at your schedule  you look at the tasks that you're  actually doing during the day and you  constantly self-audit to say is this  really the best use of my time and then  start to make adjustments based off of  that because a lot of entrepreneurs  complain that they don't have enough  time but really you're not valuing your  time enough and you're doing things that  you shouldn't be doing  [Music]  and number seven is to invest in  yourself I'd make sure that you find  time at least once a week if not every  day to invest in yourself to learn to  grow to try new things to make yourself  better because as you grow as you gain a  knowledge and experience and expertise  your business will grow and so that  could be meditation works really well  for some people it could be gratitude I  have a daily gratitude practice that I  do every single day to remind me of the  things that I have and fortunate my life  it could be watching videos to learn and  be inspired it could be reading the  could be out trying to understand the  new topic it feels you it makes you feel  better it puts you in a better mood and  it gives you more of not just the  inspiration but also the tactics of what  to do one of the things that really  helped me in my early days as an  entrepreneur was reading this book  radicals and visionaries every single  morning and it was just three of the  four pages of a different entrepreneur  that helped me get in the zone of being  inspired but also give me some tactics  of what I could do and so now I don't  want I don't read the book anymore but I  watch videos and it gives me the  motivation and also the ideas of what I  can do and so you need to make sure that  you're spending time at least every week  investing in yourself factor that in  don't let it happen by accident or  randomly on the weekend somewhere book  it into your calendar every single week  for every single day so you are  constantly learning and growing so  that's my view on the seven ways to  structure your day for success I'm  curious to figure out what did you guys  think what did you guys like the most  what did you agree with or what did you  not agree with and would you add an  eight nine ten to the list something I  missed out let me know leaving the  comments below I'm gonna join in the  discussion I also want to give a quick  shout out to Daria Bardot thank you so  much for picking up a copy of my book  your one word it really really really  really means a lot to me so thank you  guys for watching I believe in you I  hope you continue to believe in yourself  and whatever your one where it is much  love I'll see you soon

